[1] USER: this project is a url shortener web of domain https://gul.fy
    redirect this domain to localhost for test
    create text input for original url and convert to shorten link using
    base62 of that url's id in database
    that shorten link must able to edit their original link and can be set
    as active/inactive or delete it permanently
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ASSISTANT:
- Inspected the scaffolded repo (React+Vite frontend, ASP.NET Core minimal API
  backend, Npgsql/Postgres already wired up).
- Backend: added Base62.cs (encode/decode), Models.cs (DTOs), and full CRUD +
  redirect endpoints in Program.cs:
    POST   /api/urls        create short link
    GET    /api/urls        list all
    GET    /api/urls/{code} get one
    PUT    /api/urls/{code} edit originalUrl / isActive
    DELETE /api/urls/{code} permanent delete
    GET    /{code}          302 redirect / 410 inactive / 404 unknown
- Table `urls` auto-created on startup (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS).
- Frontend: built the full UI in App.tsx — input + Shorten button, list of
  links with Copy/Edit/Active toggle/Delete.
- Verified everything via curl (create/list/get/edit/toggle/delete/redirect)
  and by driving the actual UI in the Browser pane.
- Explained gul.fy local testing requires a hosts-file entry (I can't edit
  /etc/hosts myself — system-settings change) and gave the exact command to
  run: `echo "127.0.0.1 gul.fy" | sudo tee -a /etc/hosts`.

