[2] USER: so it doesn't add gul.fy... browser says "site can't be reached" /
    various follow-up questions about dotnet watch, ports, hosts file
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ASSISTANT:
- Diagnosed: hosts entry was correct; the real issue was the displayed short
  link uses no port (matches production, https://gul.fy/x) but the local API
  only listens on :5104 with no TLS — told user to hit
  `http://gul.fy:5104/{code}` when testing locally.
- Diagnosed a `dotnet watch` "Exited with error code 134" message the user
  saw — explained it was a side-effect of me killing a stale watch process
  earlier while restarting the backend to pick up code changes; confirmed
  current process was healthy and it had no effect on requests/performance.

