[13] USER: fix bug — it shouldn't count a click if the link is disabled or
     deleted
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ASSISTANT:
- Root cause: GetRedirectTarget called RecordVisit unconditionally before
  checking IsActive. Fixed by gating the RecordVisit call behind
  `if (record.IsActive)`. Deleted links were already safe (GetUrlById
  returns null, method returns before any increment).
- Verified: 3 hits while disabled left the counter unchanged; reactivating
  resumed counting correctly; deleted-link hits 404 cleanly.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[14] USER: add a button for optional custom name of the shortened link
     (e.g. gul.fy/xxx => gul.fy/Coffee)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ASSISTANT:
- New nullable `urls.custom_code` column + partial unique index (only
  enforced when non-null).
- Create/Update requests accept optional `customCode`; update semantics:
  null = untouched, "" = clear back to auto code, anything else = set/rename
  (validated against [A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}, and checked for collisions against
  both other custom codes and other links' auto-generated base62 codes).
- Code resolution (ResolveByCode) tries the custom name first, then falls
  back to decoding the code as base62 — so a link's original numeric code
  keeps working even after a custom name is set.
- Frontend: "Customize name" toggle button reveals a text input (both in the
  create form and each link's edit view); pre-fills/toggles correctly on
  edit.
- Bug found + fixed along the way: the list's post-save state update matched
  rows by `code`, which broke as soon as a save could change the code
  (exactly what renaming does). Switched all list-state matching/keying
  (React `key`, editingId tracking, update/delete filters) from `code` to
  the stable `id`.

